  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Casey Jones** (1 other source): Notes flag a disruption in the tape during Casey Jones, at about 3:01 [2]\n- **China Cat Sunflower** (1 other source): Tape deterioration is audible during China Cat Sunflower, roughly between 4:53 and 5:05, and it leads into High Time [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Next Time You See Me**: back after 143 archived shows (924 days) [9]\n- **Various Tunings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1969-09-27.early.aud.warner-jupillej.12064.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): audience recording; 9 songs; 46 min; rated 2/5 by 2 [1]\n- **gd69-09-27.aud.hanno.14857.sbeok.shnf**: audience recording; 8 songs; 46 min; rated 2.75/5 by 4 [2]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls it an audience tape that has been tweaked musically, but advises sampling before downloading; Reviewer finds the sound good for a 1969 audience tape and more listenable than other '69 audience recordings, though expectations should stay modest [3][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Banter and Bill Graham [1]\n- Reviewer says this was the period when Owsley was funding the band [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1969-09-27.early.aud.warner-jupillej.12064.sbeok.shnf**: transferred by Extraction and .shn encoding using EAC and mkwACT by Joe Jupille; source: A:?>C>CD; via Jack Warner [1]\n- **gd69-09-27.aud.hanno.14857.sbeok.shnf**: transferred by Uli Teute and Hanno Bunjes; source: Audience [2]. Also: This copy is an upgrade over the earlier circulating version (etree shn 12064), with clearer sound and less hiss and distortion [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Morrison Hotel Gallery: [Grateful Dead Triptych, Fillmore East, September 27, 1969](https://morrisonhotelgallery.com/products/grateful-dead-triptych-fillmore-east-september-27-1969-wvp6te) [10]",
